    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Discussed in https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/discussions/786\r\n\r\n<div type='discussions-op-text'>\r\n\r\n<sup>Originally posted by **ldelossa** April  7, 2024</sup>\r\nI'm wondering if this is an issue.\r\n\r\nI have auto-session working as a session manager, and I use it through mini.starter.\r\nI don't think this has to do with what session manager is in use tho. \r\n\r\nI think if you're using mini.starter and you do the following with a session manager:\r\n1. Open nvim\r\n2. Open one or two other files\r\n3. Create a source file in your repo called Starter\r\n4. Save your session\r\n\r\nWhen you go to restore this session in mini.starter I get this:\r\n\r\n```\r\nError detected while processing CursorMoved Autocommands for \"<buffer=1>\":                              \r\nError executing lua callback: ...nvim/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/starter.lua:1251: Cursor p\r\nosition outside buffer                                                                                  \r\nstack traceback:                                                                                        \r\n        [C]: in function 'nvim_win_set_cursor'                                                          \r\n        ...nvim/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/starter.lua:1251: in function 'position_cursor_o\r\nn_current_item'                                                                                         \r\n        ...nvim/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/starter.lua:1319: in function <...nvim/site/pack\r\n/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/starter.lua:1319>    \r\n``` \r\n\r\nI think mini.starter may get confused in this case. Would it make more sense to use a buffer name which starts with ```starter:///``` to ensure the starter buffer does not overlap with any files?</div>",
    "closed_at": "2024-04-08T15:29:39Z",
