    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Yes, indeed 'mini.starter' does not check existing buffers for possibly duplicating names. I can reproduce an error related to having the buffer named the same as the one in 'mini.starter', but the error is different then what what you (@idelossa) report.\r\n\r\nDoes replacing [these lines](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/d0b297ab233a57bed00ab69bd66135dee111967f/lua/mini/starter.lua#L1339-L1340) with the following one line solve the issue for you?\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n  vim.api.nvim_buf_set_name(buf_id, 'starter://' .. H.buffer_number)\r\n```",
